Primary customers are in commercial construction, HVAC, and industrial sectors across the South-Central United States. The company references work on projects throughout Northwest Arkansas and the broader region.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom welding", "Industrial welding", "HVAC ductwork fabrication", "HVAC ductwork installation", "CADD & BIM", "CAD services", "Commercial contracting"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "HVAC", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Sheet metal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom welding and industrial welding services", "CADD & BIM modeling capabilities", "HVAC ductwork fabrication and installation", "Decades of experience in South-Central construction"], "facts_used": ["Founded in early 1950s -> description", "Located in Rogers, AR -> db", "Commercial contractor fabricating and installing HVAC ductwork -> page /", "Industrial welding services -> page /", "CADD & BIM and CAD services -> page /", "Serves construction industry -> description", "Quality and good business practices philosophy -> description"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a commercial contractor, fabricating and installing HVAC ductwork systems, and doing industrial welding.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='northwest-arkansas-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Northwind Solar was established in 2007 in Amherst, Wisconsin. In 2013 the company transitioned to a worker‑owned cooperative, meaning the technicians and designers who install each system are also the owners of the business. The cooperative model was adopted to align long‑term company health with customer success.

The firm provides turnkey solar photovoltaic and battery storage solutions for residential, commercial, agricultural, nonprofit, and municipal customers across 19 counties in Central Wisconsin. Its in‑house team handles site evaluation, shade analysis, system design, financial modeling, incentive and grant applications (including Focus on Energy and USDA REAP), utility interconnection, permitting, installation, commissioning, and ongoing service. Installations are performed by NABCEP‑credentialed designers and licensed electricians, and the company has deployed megawatts of distributed solar generation since its founding.

Customers range from homeowners and family farms to businesses, schools, faith communities, and local government facilities in communities such as Wausau, Marshfield, Stevens Point, Appleton, and Oshkosh. Projects include rooftop and ground‑mount arrays, solar‑plus‑storage systems, EV charging infrastructure, and energy monitoring platforms.

Northwind Solar differentiates itself through its worker‑owned structure, which eliminates commissioned sales and ensures the same personnel support a system years after installation. The company backs its work with a 10‑year workmanship warranty, uses components from brands such as Tesla, Qcells, IronRidge, Enphase, and Franklin Whole Home, and relies heavily on referrals and repeat business.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Site evaluation and solar resource assessment", "Shade analysis", "System design and financial modeling", "Incentive and grant application (Focus on Energy, USDA REAP)", "Utility interconnection paperwork", "Permitting and inspections", "Solar PV installation (rooftop and ground-mount)", "Battery storage installation", "EV charging station installation", "Energy monitoring system installation", "System commissioning", "Ongoing service and maintenance"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Nonprofit", "Municipal", "Government", "Education", "Faith communities"], "materials": ["Solar PV modules", "Battery storage systems", "Racking systems", "Inverters", "EV chargers", "Energy monitoring systems"], "equipment": ["Tesla", "Qcells", "IronRidge", "Enphase", "Franklin Whole Home"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Worker-owned cooperative since 2013", "In-house design, installation, and service with no subcontractors", "NABCEP-certified designers and licensed electricians", "10-year workmanship warranty on all installations", "Referral-driven business model with repeat customers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007, worker-owned cooperative since 2013 -> /about", "Headquarters Amherst, Wisconsin -> db", "Services: site evaluation, design, incentives, permitting, installation, commissioning, service -> /about", "NABCEP-certified designers and licensed electricians -> /about", "10-year workmanship warranty -> /about", "Equipment brands: Tesla, Qcells, IronRidge, Enphase, Franklin Whole Home -> /about", "Industries served: residential, commercial, agricultural, nonprofit, municipal, schools, faith communities -> /about", "Service area: 19 counties in Central Wisconsin -> /about", "Megawatts of distributed solar installed -> /about", "Referral-driven, no commissioned sales -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Northwind Solar designs and installs solar power and battery storage systems for homes, farms, nonprofits, and businesses across Central Wisconsin.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='northwind-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nova Medical Inc. is headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts. The company originated from Dr. Patrick Ledden’s five years of experience designing and building custom radiofrequency (RF) coils for Massachusetts General Hospital.

The firm specializes in engineering and manufacturing medium- and high-field RF coils for magnetic resonance imaging, including head coils and custom configurations. Its roughly 10,000-square-foot facility contains a dedicated RF laboratory, design workstations running AutoCAD and SolidWorks, and 3D printing equipment for prototyping and production.

Nova Medical serves the medical imaging sector, supplying coils to hospitals and research institutions.

The company was established to translate Dr. Ledden’s coil expertise into commercial products that address specific MR imaging challenges. It emphasizes in-house design, testing, and manufacturing to deliver high-quality coils tailored to each application.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','CE Mark']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MRI coil engineering", "Custom RF coil design and manufacturing", "Head coil manufacturing", "3D printing", "RF laboratory testing", "CAD design (AutoCAD, SolidWorks)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["AutoCAD/SolidWorks design workstations", "3D printers", "RF laboratory equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom RF coil design for medium- and high-field MRI systems", "In-house RF laboratory for testing and validation", "3D printing for rapid prototyping and coil component production", "CAD-driven design using AutoCAD and SolidWorks"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded by Dr. Patrick Ledden based on his experience building custom RF coils for Massachusetts General Hospital -> page /", "Operates approximately 10,000 square feet of manufacturing space including RF laboratory, CAD workstations, and 3D printing -> page /", "Certifications: ISO 13485, CE Mark -> db", "Capabilities: MRI coil engineering, custom RF coils, 3D printing, head coils -> db", "Serves medical imaging customers such as Massachusetts General Hospital -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Nova Medical is a world renowned manufacturer of a wide variety of state-of-the-art medium and high field RF products.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nova-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='NovelCath, a Cirtec Medical company, operates from Minneapolis, Minnesota. The brand was strengthened in July 2021 when Cirtec acquired Cardea Catheter Innovations, a vertically integrated manufacturer of minimally invasive catheter devices based in San Jose, California, and folded its operations into the NovelCath name. The business focuses on the design, development, and manufacture of highly engineered catheter delivery systems for interventional medicine.

The company runs a 20,000-square-foot vertically integrated facility that houses clean-room assembly, dedicated prototyping lines, catheter assembly, extrusion, braiding, coiling, and multiple reflow technologies. Recent expansion added Nitinol processing capabilities including laser cutting, heat setting, electropolishing, EDM, 5-axis machining, and grinding. The engineering team supports customers from early-stage concept verification through animal studies and into production, emphasizing long-term manufacturability.

NovelCath serves medical-device OEMs and start-ups in three clinical areas: structural heart, electrophysiology, and neurovascular. Its product portfolio includes EP mapping and ablation catheters, structural heart valve delivery and repair systems, steerable multi-directional catheters, and neuro microcatheters. The company also produces braided and coiled reinforced sheaths, offering a range of braid patterns, wire types, and durometer configurations tailored to torque, flexibility, and tip-articulation requirements.

NovelCath differentiates itself through its vertically integrated Nitinol tubing and processing services, quick-turn prototyping, and a leadership team with over 70 years of combined experience solving complex steerable and multi-directional catheter shaft designs. As a division of Cirtec Medical, it leverages broader organizational resources while maintaining a focused, responsive approach to catheter development.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and development of interventional catheter delivery systems", "Manufacturing of catheter delivery systems", "Clean room assembly", "Dedicated prototyping lines", "Catheter assembly", "Extrusion", "Braiding", "Coiling", "Multiple reflow technologies", "Nitinol laser cutting", "Nitinol heat setting", "Electropolishing", "EDM machining", "5-axis machining", "Grinding", "Quick-turn prototyping", "Design consultation", "Animal study support", "Braid and coil pattern configuration", "Braid density 15-200 PPI", "8, 16, 32 filament braiding", "Round or flat wire braiding", "Single or multi-variable durometer", "Braid to coil transition"], "industries": ["Structural Heart", "Electrophysiology", "Neurovascular"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Nitinol", "Polymer fibers", "PTFE", "Nylon", "Polyimide", "Pebax", "Round wire", "Flat wire"], "equipment": ["5-axis machining centers", "EDM machines", "Laser cutting systems", "Electropolishing equipment", "Grinding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated Nitinol tubing and processing", "Quick-turn prototyping for catheter designs", "In-house extrusion, braiding, coiling, and assembly", "70+ years combined team experience in steerable catheter shafts", "Focus on structural heart, electrophysiology, and neurovascular delivery systems"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Minneapolis, MN -> /", "20,000 sq ft vertically integrated facility -> /", "Contract manufacturer of catheter delivery systems -> /", "Specializes in structural heart, electrophysiology, neurovascular -> /", "Team with 70+ years combined experience -> /", "In-house extrusion, braiding, coiling, assembly -> /capabilities", "Nitinol processing: laser-cutting, heat-setting, electropolishing, EDM, 5-axis machining, grinding -> /capabilities", "Quick-turn prototyping for catheter designs -> /capabilities", "Acquired Cardea Catheter Innovations in July 2021 -> db", "Parent company Cirtec Medical -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "NovelCath is a contract manufacturer of highly engineered catheter delivery systems based in Minneapolis, MN.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='novelcath-a-cirtec-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='O''Meara Solar is based in East Orange, Vermont. The company was founded as a father-son partnership between Darren O''Meara and Patrick O''Meara after they spent the better part of a decade installing, maintaining, and living with solar energy in their own homes and woodworking shop.

The firm designs, sells, installs, and services grid-tie, off-grid, and grid-tie-with-battery-backup solar photovoltaic systems. It also operates a solar-powered woodworking shop where it builds custom enclosures, cabinets, furniture, and built-ins using locally sustainably harvested wood. The company is commercially insured and draws on a network of master electricians and concrete professionals for structural work.

O''Meara Solar serves residential customers in Orange County, Vermont, and Grafton County, New Hampshire, as well as surrounding areas. Its off-grid systems are designed for remote homes and cabins, accommodating 120/240 V loads such as deep-well pumps and shop tools.

The business grew directly from the founders'' personal off-grid lifestyle; Darren O''Meara holds a NABCEP Photovoltaic EL certification and handles electrical design, while Patrick O''Meara brings over thirty years of construction and fine woodworking experience.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Photovoltaic EL']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Solar PV installation", "Solar PV maintenance and service", "Grid-tie solar system installation", "Off-grid solar system installation", "Grid-tie with battery backup installation", "Custom woodworking", "Cabinet making", "Furniture making", "Built-in furniture fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Off-grid solar", "Custom woodworking"], "materials": ["Wood (locally sustainably harvested)", "Solar modules", "Racking", "Inverters", "Batteries"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dealer access to major solar equipment manufacturers", "Commercially insured with network of master electricians and concrete professionals", "First-hand off-grid living experience informs system design", "Solar-powered woodworking shop using locally harvested wood", "NABCEP Photovoltaic EL certified design expertise"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: East Orange, Vermont -> db", "Founders: Darren O''Meara and Patrick O''Meara -> /about", "Family-owned father-son partnership -> /about", "Services: Solar PV design, installation, service for grid-tie, off-grid, battery backup -> /", "Woodworking: custom enclosures, cabinets, furniture -> /", "Certification: NABCEP Photovoltaic EL exam passed by Darren -> /about", "Dealer for large solar distributors -> /about", "Commercially insured with subcontractor network -> /about", "Solar-powered woodworking shop -> /", "Locally sustainably harvested wood -> /", "Service area: Orange County VT, Grafton County NH -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Design, Sales, Installation, and Service of Solar PV. Grid-tie, off-grid, and grid-tie with battery backup solutions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='o-meara-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='OAI Electronics operates from Tulsa, Oklahoma, where it runs two environmentally monitored facilities totaling 65,000 square feet.

As a build-to-print contract electronics manufacturer, OAI produces circuit card assemblies, flex and rigid-flex assemblies, and electromechanical enclosures. Its capabilities span surface-mount and through-hole PCB assembly, RF boards, high-temperature assemblies, potting, encapsulation, conformal coating, and system integration, all performed to IPC-A-610 and IPC J-STD-001 Classes 2 and 3.

The company serves the aerospace, military, medical, and industrial sectors, with its ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certification scope explicitly covering printed circuit board assemblies and box builds for those markets.

