UPDATE companies SET description='Okuhara Foods Inc. operates from Honolulu, Hawaii, where it was founded in 1946 as a family-owned business. The company began as a modest operation producing fishcake, a traditional Japanese staple made from pureed white fish that is seasoned, shaped, and steamed until firm.

Today, the manufacturer produces a range of seafood-based products including its signature fishcake (kamaboko), customer-favorite Misoyaki Butterfish, and pre-marinated salmon fillets. The production process centers on fish pureeing, seasoning, forming, and steaming, along with marination and ready-to-cook meal preparation. Products are packaged for retail distribution.

Okuhara Foods supplies grocery retailers across Hawaii, with its products stocked at chains such as Times, Don Quijote, Marukai, and Big Save.

